WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.845 --> 00:00:04.262
- [Narrator] This is the collared lizard.

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:09.045
The two black bands around
their neck give them their name.

00:00:09.045 --> 00:00:11.872
Collared lizards can actually
run on their hind legs

00:00:11.872 --> 00:00:14.688
and reach up to 15 miles per hour.

00:00:14.688 --> 00:00:16.853
Their tails are used
for balancing themselves

00:00:16.853 --> 00:00:19.124
when they are up and sprinting.

00:00:19.124 --> 00:00:20.831
They are a medium-size lizard,

00:00:20.831 --> 00:00:23.381
reaching up to a foot
and a half in length.

00:00:23.381 --> 00:00:26.304
Native to western North
America, they prefer to live

00:00:26.304 --> 00:00:29.387
in rocky habitats with sparse vegetation.

00:00:29.387 --> 00:00:31.317
Today they are widespread,

00:00:31.317 --> 00:00:34.921
but only a few decades ago
their population was declining.

00:00:34.921 --> 00:00:37.291
Clearing land as a form of fire prevention

00:00:37.291 --> 00:00:40.341
has greatly helped its population rebound,

00:00:40.341 --> 00:00:43.945
as they need open, rocky
habitats to survive.

00:00:43.945 --> 00:00:45.861
This is the collared lizard.

00:00:45.861 --> 00:00:49.111
(cheerful piano music)

